  3908 |             config (`Union[PreTrainedConfig, str, os.PathLike]`, *optional*):
  3909 |                 Can be either:
  3910 | 
  3911 |                     - an instance of a class derived from [`PreTrainedConfig`],
  3912 |                     - a string or path valid as input to [`~PreTrainedConfig.from_pretrained`].
  3913 | 
  3914 |                 Configuration for the model to use instead of an automatically loaded configuration. Configuration can
  3915 |                 be automatically loaded when:
  3916 | 
  3917 |                     - The model is a model provided by the library (loaded with the *model id* string of a pretrained
  3918 |                       model).
  3919 |                     - The model was saved using [`~PreTrainedModel.save_pretrained`] and is reloaded by supplying the
  3920 |                       save directory.
  3921 |                     - The model is loaded by supplying a local directory as `pretrained_model_name_or_path` and a
  3922 |                       configuration JSON file named *config.json* is found in the directory.
  3923 |             state_dict (`dict[str, torch.Tensor]`, *optional*):
  3924 |                 A state dictionary to use instead of a state dictionary loaded from saved weights file.
  3925 | 
  3926 |                 This option can be used if you want to create a model from a pretrained configuration but load your own
  3927 |                 weights. In this case though, you should check if using [`~PreTrainedModel.save_pretrained`] and
  3928 |                 [`~PreTrainedModel.from_pretrained`] is not a simpler option.
  3929 |             cache_dir (`Union[str, os.PathLike]`, *optional*):
  3930 |                 Path to a directory in which a downloaded pretrained model configuration should be cached if the
  3931 |                 standard cache should not be used.
  3932 |             ignore_mismatched_sizes (`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`):
  3933 |                 Whether or not to raise an error if some of the weights from the checkpoint do not have the same size
  3934 |                 as the weights of the model (if for instance, you are instantiating a model with 10 labels from a
  3935 |                 checkpoint with 3 labels).
  3936 |             force_download (`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`):
  3937 |                 Whether or not to force the (re-)download of the model weights and configuration files, overriding the
  3938 |                 cached versions if they exist.
  3939 |             proxies (`dict[str, str]`, *optional*):
  3940 |                 A dictionary of proxy servers to use by protocol or endpoint, e.g., `{'http': 'foo.bar:3128',
  3941 |                 'http://hostname': 'foo.bar:4012'}`. The proxies are used on each request.
  3942 |             output_loading_info(`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`):
  3943 |                 Whether or not to also return a dictionary containing missing keys, unexpected keys and error messages.
  3944 |             local_files_only(`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`):
  3945 |                 Whether or not to only look at local files (i.e., do not try to download the model).
  3946 |             token (`str` or `bool`, *optional*):
  3947 |                 The token to use as HTTP bearer authorization for remote files. If `True`, or not specified, will use
  3948 |                 the token generated when running `hf auth login` (stored in `~/.huggingface`).
  3949 |             revision (`str`, *optional*, defaults to `"main"`):
  3950 |                 The specific model version to use. It can be a branch name, a tag name, or a commit id, since we use a
  3951 |                 git-based system for storing models and other artifacts on huggingface.co, so `revision` can be any
  3952 |                 identifier allowed by git.
  3953 | 
  3954 |                 <Tip>
  3955 | 
  3956 |                 To test a pull request you made on the Hub, you can pass `revision="refs/pr/<pr_number>"`.
  3957 | 
  3958 |                 </Tip>
  3959 |             attn_implementation (`str`, *optional*):
  3960 |                 The attention implementation to use in the model (if relevant). Can be any of
  3961 |                     - `"eager"` (manual implementation of the attention)
  3962 |                     - `"sdpa"` (using [`F.scaled_dot_product_attention`](https://pytorch.org/docs/master/generated/torch.nn.functional.scaled_dot_product_attention.html))
  3963 |                     - `"flash_attention_2"` (using [Dao-AILab/flash-attention](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention))
  3964 |                     - `"flash_attention_3"` (using [Dao-AILab/flash-attention/hopper](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/tree/main/hopper))
  3965 |                     - `"flash_attention_4"` (using [Dao-AILab/flash-attention/flash_attn/cute](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/tree/main/flash_attn/cute)).
  3966 |                 By default, if available, SDPA will be used. The default is otherwise the manual `"eager"` implementation.
  3967 | 
  3968 |                 Accept HF kernel references in the form:
  3969 |                   <namespace>/<repo_name>[@<revision>][:<kernel_name>]
  3970 | 
  3971 |                 - <namespace> and <repo_name> are any non-"/" and non-":" sequences.
  3972 |                 - "@<revision>" is optional (branch, tag, or commit-ish), e.g. "@main", "@v1.2.0", "@abc123".
  3973 |                 - ":<kernel_name>" is optional and selects a function inside the kernel repo.
  3974 |                 - Both options can appear together and in this order only: @revision first, then :kernel_name.
  3975 |                 - We intentionally allow a leading "<wrapper>|" prefix (e.g., "flash|...") because the code
  3976 |                   strips it before loading; '|' is not excluded in the character classes here.
  3977 | 
  3978 |                 Examples that match:
  3979 |                   "org/model"
  3980 |                   "org/model@main"
  3981 |                   "org/model:custom_kernel"
  3982 |                   "org/model@v1.2.3:custom_kernel"
  3983 |             experts_implementation (`str`, *optional*):
