   559 |         """
   560 |         Generates text using the diffusion model.
   561 | 
   562 |         It contains an outer loop doing autoregressive generation of canvases (blocks of tokens), and an inner
   563 |         loop doing diffusion on each canvas. The algorithm works roughly as follows:
   564 |         ```
   565 |         1. Autoregressive canvas generation loop:
   566 |             a. Encode all previous tokens using the encoder, to get the KV cache.
   567 |             b. Prepare data for the new denoising loop
   568 |             c. For each denoising (diffusion) step:
   569 |                 i.   Run the decoder, taking the current canvas, the encoder KV cache, and the self-conditioning logits
   570 |                      (if available) as inputs.
   571 |                 ii.  Select new canvas tokens from the output logits.
   572 |                 iii. Apply the sampler acceptance and renoising logic.
   573 |                 iv.  Update the diffusion stopping criteria.
   574 |                 v.   Use the output logits as self-conditioning logits for the next step.
   575 |             d. Append the new denoised canvas to the sequence of generated tokens.
   576 |             e. Check if any autoregressive stopping criteria are met, and break the outer loop if all sequences have
   577 |                met them. Replaces generated tokens in finished sequences by pad.
   578 |             f. Prepare tensors for the next block
   579 |         ```
