  1145 |                 `special_tokens_dict`. Otherwise, `extra_special_tokens` will be extended. In the former
  1146 |                 case, the tokens will NOT be removed from the tokenizer's full vocabulary - they are only being flagged
  1147 |                 as non-special tokens. Remember, this only affects which tokens are skipped during decoding, not the
  1148 |                 `added_tokens_encoder` and `added_tokens_decoder`. This means that the previous
  1149 |                 `extra_special_tokens` are still added tokens, and will not be split by the model.
  1150 | 
  1151 |         Returns:
  1152 |             `int`: Number of tokens added to the vocabulary.
  1153 | 
