  2203 |                 the [`~Trainer.model_init`] function to instantiate the model if it has some randomly initialized
  2204 |                 parameters.
  2205 |             gradient_checkpointing (`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`):
  2206 |                 If True, use gradient checkpointing to save memory at the expense of slower backward pass.
  2207 | 
  2208 |         Example:
  2209 | 
  2210 |         ```py
  2211 |         >>> from transformers import TrainingArguments
  2212 | 
  2213 |         >>> args = TrainingArguments("working_dir")
  2214 |         >>> args = args.set_training(learning_rate=1e-4, batch_size=32)
  2215 |         >>> args.learning_rate
  2216 |         1e-4
  2217 |         ```
  2218 |         """
  2219 |         self.do_train = True
  2220 |         self.learning_rate = learning_rate
  2221 |         self.per_device_train_batch_size = batch_size
  2222 |         self.weight_decay = weight_decay
  2223 |         self.num_train_epochs = num_epochs
  2224 |         self.max_steps = max_steps
  2225 |         self.gradient_accumulation_steps = gradient_accumulation_steps
  2226 |         self.seed = seed
  2227 |         self.gradient_checkpointing = gradient_checkpointing
