   345 |     A model class should inherit from `GenerationMixin` to enable calling methods like `generate`, or when it
   346 |     has defined a custom `generate` method that relies on `GenerationMixin`, directly or indirectly, which
   347 |     approximately shares the same interface to public methods like `generate`. Three examples:
   348 |         - `LlamaForCausalLM` should inherit from `GenerationMixin` to enable calling `generate` and other public
   349 |             methods in the mixin;
   350 |         - `BlipForQuestionAnswering` has a custom `generate` method that approximately shares the same interface as
   351 |            `GenerationMixin.generate` (it has a few extra arguments, and the same output). That function also calls
   352 |            `GenerationMixin.generate` indirectly, through an inner model. As such, `BlipForQuestionAnswering` should
   353 |            inherit from `GenerationMixin` to benefit from all generation-related automation in our codebase;
   354 |         - `BarkModel` has a custom `generate` method and one of its inner models calls `GenerationMixin.generate`.
   355 |             However, its `generate` does not share the same interface as `GenerationMixin.generate`. In this case,
   356 |             `BarkModel` should NOT inherit from `GenerationMixin`, as it breaks the `generate` interface.
