  2286 |                 provided no constraint is applied. This function takes 2 arguments: the batch ID `batch_id` and
  2287 |                 `input_ids`. It has to return a list with the allowed tokens for the next generation step conditioned
  2288 |                 on the batch ID `batch_id` and the previously generated tokens `inputs_ids`. This argument is useful
  2289 |                 for constrained generation conditioned on the prefix, as described in [Autoregressive Entity
  2290 |                 Retrieval](https://huggingface.co/papers/2010.00904).
