  2595 |         <Tip>
  2596 | 
  2597 |         If the `encoded_inputs` passed are dictionary of numpy arrays, or PyTorch tensors, the
  2598 |         result will use the same type unless you provide a different tensor type with `return_tensors`. In the case of
  2599 |         PyTorch tensors, you will lose the specific device of your tensors however.
  2600 | 
  2601 |         </Tip>
  2602 | 
  2603 |         Args:
  2604 |             encoded_inputs ([`BatchEncoding`], list of [`BatchEncoding`], `dict[str, list[int]]`, `dict[str, list[list[int]]` or `list[dict[str, list[int]]]`):
  2605 |                 Tokenized inputs. Can represent one input ([`BatchEncoding`] or `dict[str, list[int]]`) or a batch of
  2606 |                 tokenized inputs (list of [`BatchEncoding`], *dict[str, list[list[int]]]* or *list[dict[str,
  2607 |                 list[int]]]*) so you can use this method during preprocessing as well as in a PyTorch Dataloader
  2608 |                 collate function.
