  2863 |         using the tokenizer and vocabulary with options to remove special tokens and clean up
  2864 |         tokenization spaces.
  2865 | 
  2866 |         Similar to doing `self.convert_tokens_to_string(self.convert_ids_to_tokens(token_ids))`.
  2867 | 
  2868 |         Args:
  2869 |             token_ids (`Union[int, list[int], list[list[int]], np.ndarray, torch.Tensor]`):
  2870 |                 A single sequence or a batch (list of sequences) of tokenized input ids. Can be obtained using the
  2871 |                 `__call__` method.
  2872 |             skip_special_tokens (`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`):
  2873 |                 Whether or not to remove special tokens in the decoding.
  2874 |             kwargs (additional keyword arguments, *optional*):
  2875 |                 Will be passed to the underlying model specific decode method.
  2876 | 
  2877 |         Returns:
  2878 |             `Union[str, list[str]]`: The decoded string for a single sequence, or a list of decoded strings for a
  2879 |             batch of sequences.
