  1427 | class DynamicCache(Cache):
  1428 |     """
  1429 |     A cache that grows dynamically as more tokens are generated. This is the default for generative models.
  1430 |     It stores the key and value states as a list of `CacheLayer`, one for each layer. The expected shape for each tensor
  1431 |     in the `CacheLayer`s is `[batch_size, num_heads, seq_len, head_dim]`.
  1432 |     If a config is passed, it will additionally check for sliding or hybrid cache structure, greatly reducing the
  1433 |     memory requirement of the cached tensors to `[batch_size, num_heads, min(seq_len, sliding_window), head_dim]`.
  1434 | 
  1435 |     See `Cache` for details on common methods that are implemented by all cache classes.
  1436 | 
  1437 |     Args:
  1438 |         ddp_cache_data (`Iterable[tuple[torch.Tensor, torch.Tensor]]`, *optional*):
  1439 |             It was originally added for compatibility with `torch.distributed` (DDP). In a nutshell, it is
  1440 |             `map(gather_map, zip(*caches))`, i.e. each item in the iterable contains the key and value states
  1441 |             for a layer gathered across replicas by torch.distributed (shape=[global batch size, num_heads, seq_len, head_dim]).
  1442 |             Note: it needs to be the 1st arg as well to work correctly
  1443 |         config (`PreTrainedConfig`, *optional*):
  1444 |             The config of the model for which this Cache will be used. If passed, it will be used to check for sliding
  1445 |             or hybrid layer structure, greatly reducing the memory requirement of the cached tensors to
  1446 |             `[batch_size, num_heads, min(seq_len, sliding_window), head_dim]`.
  1447 |         offloading (`bool`, *optional*, defaults to `False`):
