  3948 |                 the token generated when running `hf auth login` (stored in `~/.huggingface`).
  3949 |             revision (`str`, *optional*, defaults to `"main"`):
  3950 |                 The specific model version to use. It can be a branch name, a tag name, or a commit id, since we use a
  3951 |                 git-based system for storing models and other artifacts on huggingface.co, so `revision` can be any
  3952 |                 identifier allowed by git.
  3953 | 
  3954 |                 <Tip>
  3955 | 
  3956 |                 To test a pull request you made on the Hub, you can pass `revision="refs/pr/<pr_number>"`.
  3957 | 
  3958 |                 </Tip>
  3959 |             attn_implementation (`str`, *optional*):
  3960 |                 The attention implementation to use in the model (if relevant). Can be any of
  3961 |                     - `"eager"` (manual implementation of the attention)
  3962 |                     - `"sdpa"` (using [`F.scaled_dot_product_attention`](https://pytorch.org/docs/master/generated/torch.nn.functional.scaled_dot_product_attention.html))
  3963 |                     - `"flash_attention_2"` (using [Dao-AILab/flash-attention](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention))
  3964 |                     - `"flash_attention_3"` (using [Dao-AILab/flash-attention/hopper](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/tree/main/hopper))
  3965 |                     - `"flash_attention_4"` (using [Dao-AILab/flash-attention/flash_attn/cute](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/tree/main/flash_attn/cute)).
  3966 |                 By default, if available, SDPA will be used. The default is otherwise the manual `"eager"` implementation.
  3967 | 
  3968 |                 Accept HF kernel references in the form:
  3969 |                   <namespace>/<repo_name>[@<revision>][:<kernel_name>]
  3970 | 
  3971 |                 - <namespace> and <repo_name> are any non-"/" and non-":" sequences.
  3972 |                 - "@<revision>" is optional (branch, tag, or commit-ish), e.g. "@main", "@v1.2.0", "@abc123".
  3973 |                 - ":<kernel_name>" is optional and selects a function inside the kernel repo.
  3974 |                 - Both options can appear together and in this order only: @revision first, then :kernel_name.
  3975 |                 - We intentionally allow a leading "<wrapper>|" prefix (e.g., "flash|...") because the code
  3976 |                   strips it before loading; '|' is not excluded in the character classes here.
  3977 | 
  3978 |                 Examples that match:
  3979 |                   "org/model"
  3980 |                   "org/model@main"
  3981 |                   "org/model:custom_kernel"
  3982 |                   "org/model@v1.2.3:custom_kernel"
  3983 |             experts_implementation (`str`, *optional*):
  3984 |                 The experts implementation to use in the model (if relevant). Can be any of:
  3985 | 
  3986 |                 - `"eager"` (sequential implementation of the experts matrix multiplications).
  3987 |                 - `"batched_mm"` (using [`torch.bmm`](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.bmm.html)).
  3988 |                 - `"grouped_mm"` (using [`torch.nn.functional.grouped_mm`](https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/main/generated/torch.nn.functional.grouped_mm.html)).
  3989 | 
  3990 |                 By default, if the model supports it, `"grouped_mm"` will be used. The default is otherwise the manual `"eager"` implementation.
  3991 | 
  3992 |             > Parameters for big model inference
  3993 | 
  3994 |             dtype (`str` or `torch.dtype`, *optional*, defaults to `"auto"`):
  3995 |                 Override the default `torch_dtype` and load the model under a specific `dtype`. The different options
  3996 |                 are:
  3997 | 
  3998 |                 1. `torch.float16` or `torch.bfloat16` or `torch.float`: load in a specified
  3999 |                   `dtype`, ignoring the model's `config.dtype` if one exists. If not specified
  4000 |                   - the model will get loaded in `torch.float` (fp32).
  4001 | 
  4002 |                 2. `"auto"` - A `dtype` or `torch_dtype` entry in the `config.json` file of the model will be
  4003 |                   attempted to be used. If this entry isn't found then next check the `dtype` of the first weight in
  4004 |                   the checkpoint that's of a floating point type and use that as `dtype`. This will load the model
  4005 |                   using the `dtype` it was saved in at the end of the training. It can't be used as an indicator of how
  4006 |                   the model was trained. Since it could be trained in one of half precision dtypes, but saved in fp32.
  4007 | 
  4008 |                 3. A string that is a valid `torch.dtype`. E.g. "float32" loads the model in `torch.float32`, "float16" loads in `torch.float16` etc.
  4009 | 
  4010 |                 <Tip>
  4011 | 
  4012 |                 For some models the `dtype` they were trained in is unknown - you may try to check the model's paper or
  4013 |                 reach out to the authors and ask them to add this information to the model's card and to insert the
  4014 |                 `dtype` or `torch_dtype` entry in `config.json` on the hub.
