  1426 |     r"""
  1427 |     We build a mapping from the keys obtained by renaming each of the checkpoint keys according to the weight_mapping rules.
  1428 |     Then we load the tensors into the model, applying any conversion operations as needed.
  1429 | 
  1430 |     The `param_name_to_load` will look like this:
  1431 |     {
  1432 |         "model.layers.0.attention.q.weight": # Notice here there is only the first key of the target keys
  1433 |             WeightConverter(
  1434 |                 source_patterns=["qkv"],
  1435 |                 target_patterns=["q", "k","v"],
  1436 |                 operations=[Chunk(dim=0, chunks=3)]),
  1437 |                 collected_tensors={
  1438 |                     "qkv": [Future]},
  1439 |                 layer_targets={
  1440 |                     "model.layers.0.attention.q.weight": {"model.layers.0.attention.qkv.weight"},
  1441 |                     "model.layers.0.attention.k.weight": {"model.layers.0.attention.qkv.weight"},
  1442 |                     "model.layers.0.attention.v.weight": {"model.layers.0.attention.qkv.weight"},
  1443 |                 }
  1444 |             ),
  1445 |         ...
  1446 |     }
  1447 | 
  1448 |     We make sure that the keys are the full keys. The only "nit" here is that 1 key can map to multiple target keys (e.g. qkv -> q, k, v).
  1449 |     In that case the weight converter will take care of doing the appropriate renaming.
  1450 | 
  1451 |     For example for:
  1452 |     ```python
  1453 |     WeightConverter(
  1454 |         source_patterns=["mlp.experts.*.gate_proj.weight","mlp.experts.*.up_proj.weight"],
  1455 |         target_patterns="mlp.experts.gate_up_proj",
  1456 |         operations=[MergeModulelist(dim=0), Concatenate(dim=1)],
  1457 |     )
  1458 |     ```
  1459 |     we would have the following collected tensors:
  1460 |     ```python
  1461 |     collected_tensors = {
  1462 |         "mlp.experts.*.gate_proj.weight": [Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future],
  1463 |         "mlp.experts.*.up_proj.weight": [Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future],
  1464 |     }
  1465 |     ```
  1466 |     The first op, `MergeModulelist`, would stack the 8 tensors of each source but will not "rename" them into the fused target name.
  1467 |     The second op, `Concatenate`, would then rename the fused tensor into the final target name.
  1468 | 
  1469 |     If we want to split `qkv` we would have:
  1470 |     ```python
  1471 |     collected_tensors = {
  1472 |         "attention.qkv.weight": [Future], # here its the full SOURCE keys.
  1473 |     }
