    37 | class DtensorShardOperation:
    38 |     """Shard-on-read: slice a full disk tensor down to this rank's local
    39 |     DTensor shard, for any combination of placements on a 1-D or n-D mesh.  It's on
    40 |     read because instructions are made so the cpu only fetches on disk the parts we want.
    41 | 
    42 |     Placements primer
    43 |     -----------------
    44 |     Each mesh dim carries one placement describing how it slices the tensor:
    45 | 
    46 |     | Placement                | Local data on each rank of the mesh dim         |
    47 |     |--------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|
    48 |     | Replicate                | full tensor (no slicing)                        |
    49 |     | Shard(d)                 | contiguous chunk of dim d (rows r*c .. (r+1)*c) |
    50 |     | _StridedShard(d, sf=N)   | one chunk from each of N groups along dim d,   |
    51 |     |                          | concatenated together (interleaved layout)      |
    52 | 
    53 |     Different scenarios of different placements
    54 |     ------------------------------------------
    55 |     Placement tuples are ordered outermost-first; for a 2-D (fsdp, tp) mesh
    56 |     the tuple is (fsdp_placement, tp_placement).
    57 | 
    58 |     | Scenario                                          | Placements                                  |
    59 |     |---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
    60 |     | TP-only, non-fused (e.g. q_proj/k_proj/v_proj)    | [Shard(d)]                                   |
    61 |     | TP-only, fused gate/up                            | [_StridedShard(d, sf=2)]                     |
    62 |     | TP + FSDP, same tensor dim (contiguous TP case)   | [Shard(d), Shard(d)]                         |
    63 |     | TP + FSDP, same tensor dim (fused/interleaved TP) | [_StridedShard(d, sf=tp_size), Shard(d)]     |
    64 |     | TP + FSDP, different dims                         | [Shard(d1), Shard(d2)]                       |
    65 | 
    66 |     Loading (this class)
    67 |     --------------------
    68 |     During from_pretrained, each rank looks up every tensor key, but does not load the weight bytes yet (safetensors get_slice).
    69 |     When a weight is needed, shard_tensor indexes that slice to read only this rank's local shard through Dtensor logic which provides
    70 |     placement logics
    71 | 
    72 |     Depending on how the checkpoint was saved, the weight loader either gives us one big tensor or many small ones:
    73 | 
    74 |     1. One stacked tensor: the checkpoint has one key with all experts together, shaped [num_experts, in, out].
    75 |        The weight loader passes it straight through; we slice out this rank's piece.
    76 | 
    77 |     2. One tensor per expert:  the checkpoint has a separate key for each expert (expert 0, expert 1, …), each shaped [in, out].
    78 |        The weight loader feeds them in one at a time. If this rank doesn't own a given expert,
    79 |        we skip it. Later, `MergeModulelist` will stack the owned expert we kept to create the rank's local shard
    80 |     """
    81 | 
