  1232 |     r"""
  1233 |     We build a mapping from the keys obtained by renaming each of the checkpoint keys according to the weight_mapping rules.
  1234 |     Then we load the tensors into the model, applying any conversion operations as needed.
  1235 | 
  1236 |     The `param_name_to_load` will look like this:
  1237 |     {
  1238 |         "model.layers.0.attention.q.weight": # Notice here there is only the first key of the target keys
  1239 |             WeightConverter(
  1240 |                 source_patterns=["qkv"],
  1241 |                 target_patterns=["q", "k","v"],
  1242 |                 operations=[Chunk(dim=0, chunks=3)]),
  1243 |                 collected_tensors={
  1244 |                     "qkv": [Future]},
  1245 |                 layer_targets={
  1246 |                     "model.layers.0.attention.q.weight": {"model.layers.0.attention.qkv.weight"},
  1247 |                     "model.layers.0.attention.k.weight": {"model.layers.0.attention.qkv.weight"},
  1248 |                     "model.layers.0.attention.v.weight": {"model.layers.0.attention.qkv.weight"},
  1249 |                 }
  1250 |             ),
  1251 |         ...
  1252 |     }
  1253 | 
  1254 |     We make sure that the keys are the full keys. The only "nit" here is that 1 key can map to multiple target keys (e.g. qkv -> q, k, v).
  1255 |     In that case the weight converter will take care of doing the appropriate renaming.
  1256 | 
  1257 |     For example for:
  1258 |     ```python
  1259 |     WeightConverter(
  1260 |         source_patterns=["mlp.experts.*.gate_proj.weight","mlp.experts.*.up_proj.weight"],
  1261 |         target_patterns="mlp.experts.gate_up_proj",
  1262 |         operations=[MergeModulelist(dim=0), Concatenate(dim=1)],
  1263 |     )
  1264 |     ```
  1265 |     we would have the following collected tensors:
  1266 |     ```python
  1267 |     collected_tensors = {
  1268 |         "mlp.experts.*.gate_proj.weight": [Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future],
  1269 |         "mlp.experts.*.up_proj.weight": [Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future, Future],
  1270 |     }
  1271 |     ```
